🚀 MERN Stack Blogging Platform - Backend Documentation
This repository contains the industrial-standard backend for a full-stack blogging application. It is built using the MVC (Model-View-Controller) architecture to ensure scalability, security, and performance.

🛠 Tech Stack
Node.js & Express.js: Server-side runtime and framework.

MongoDB & Mongoose: NoSQL database and Object Data Modeling (ODM).

JWT (JSON Web Tokens): Secure user authentication.

Bcrypt: Password hashing for data privacy.

Cloudinary: Cloud-based image management for banners and profile pictures.

Nanoid: For generating short, unique, and SEO-friendly URL slugs.

📂 Project Architecture
The project follows a modular structure to keep the code clean and maintainable.

Plaintext
backend/
├── controllers/    # Business logic (Auth, Blog, User, Notification)
├── middleware/     # Security gates (verifyJWT)
├── models/         # Database schemas (User, Blog, Notification, Comment)
├── routes/         # API endpoint definitions
├── utils/          # Helper functions (Cloudinary upload)
├── .env            # Private environment variables
└── server.js       # Entry point of the application
🔐 Core Features & Logic
1. Authentication System
We use a dual-layer security approach:

Registration: Validates email/password and hashes the password using Bcrypt before saving to MongoDB.

Login: Compares hashed passwords and generates a JWT that contains the user's unique ID.

Access Control: A verifyJWT middleware intercepts requests to private routes, ensuring only logged-in users can post or comment.

2. Blogging Engine
Drafts vs. Published: Users can save progress as drafts. Validation only triggers when the draft flag is false.

SEO Slugs: Titles are transformed into URL-friendly strings (e.g., "My First Blog" → my-first-blog-k3p91).

Pagination: To handle high traffic, the server only sends 5 blogs at a time using .skip() and .limit().

3. Engagement & Notifications
Like Toggle: Atomic updates using $inc to prevent data races.

Comment System: Supports parent-child relationships for nested replies.

Automated Triggers: Notifications are automatically created for likes, comments, and replies.

📡 API Endpoints
Auth Routes (/api/auth)
Method	Endpoint	Description	Access
POST	/signup	Register a new user	Public
POST	/signin	Login and receive JWT	Public
Blog Routes (/api/blog)
Method	Endpoint	Description	Access
POST	/create-blog	Create a new post or draft	Private
POST	/latest-blogs	Get recent posts (Paginated)	Public
POST	/search-blogs	Search by title or tag	Public
POST	/like-blog	Toggle like on a post	Private
POST	/add-comment	Add comment or reply	Private
User Routes (/api/user)
Method	Endpoint	Description	Access
POST	/get-profile	Fetch user info & their blogs	Public
POST	/update-profile	Update bio & social links	Private
⚙️ Setup & Installation
Clone the project and enter the backend directory.

Install dependencies:

Bash
npm install
Configure Environment Variables: Create a .env file:

Code snippet
PORT=3000
MONGO_URL=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_random_secret_string
CLOUDINARY_NAME=your_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_secret
Run the server:

Bash
npm start
🛡 Security Best Practices Implemented
Password Hashing: Never storing plain-text passwords.

JWT Stateless Auth: Secure sessions without slowing down the database.

Regex Sanitization: Preventing malicious characters in URL slugs.

CORS Protection: Restricting API access to trusted origins.

Data Exclusion: Using .select("-password") to never leak sensitive data in API responses.

